Significance: patch
Type: dev
Comment: Fixes found reviewing the Back In Stock Notifications migration: the run lock is now handed back when a CLI run halts on an error and reclaimed when the batch watchdog kills a background run, a failed run is reported as failed on the Tools screen instead of looking paused, known losses accumulate across the separate requests a background run uses, the legacy-link shim is only switched on once a batch has committed, the product-meta section can no longer strand a product that becomes a candidate mid-run or lose a whole batch to one throwing save (its failure marker is now written outside the product CRUD layer, so recovery never repeats the save that failed), a section whose rows can be neither migrated nor marked is set aside and reported rather than served forever, the product-meta candidate query is driven off the legacy meta rows themselves instead of joining products and orders its batch in PHP so the index it needs is actually used, a product whose Core sign-up flag has already been set is left alone rather than overwritten, trashed products migrate so restoring one does not silently re-enable sign-ups, and an adoption that leaves a subscriber less live than they were is reported rather than counted as a plain success. Reachable only while the migration feature is on.
